204:PROVED, quantitative loss accounting: if a particular cluster polynomial has a negative value at most −b times its size ell, and the rest contributes at most E at that same angle, then M>=b ell−E. This beats c sqrt(n) only if ell>=(c sqrt(n)+E)/b. For E=O(sqrt(n)) the threshold is of order sqrt(n). Without control of E, even ell~n^(5/6) need not force M of order ell. There is no valid extraction-to-Gibbs theorem proved here.

